+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Ensure Flask context teardown completes registered cleanup despite individual
+cleanup failures and reports those failures only after context cleanup.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Teardown completes best-effort cleanup
+During request and application-context teardown, Flask MUST invoke every
+registered teardown callback in its existing order and MUST send the matching
+teardown signal even if preceding teardown callbacks or signal receivers raise.
+After all teardown work has been attempted, Flask MUST raise the collected
+teardown failures. On Python versions with exception groups, the raised error
+MUST preserve every collected failure; on older Python versions, Flask MAY
+raise the first collected failure.
+
+#### Scenario: Multiple request teardown callbacks fail
+- **WHEN** more than one request teardown callback raises during context pop
+- **THEN** later callbacks and the request teardown signal are invoked before
+  the collected teardown failures are raised
+
+#### Scenario: Application teardown signal receiver fails
+- **WHEN** an application-context teardown signal receiver raises
+- **THEN** Flask finishes attempting the signal's remaining receivers and
+  raises the collected failure after callbacks and receivers complete
+
+### Requirement: Context state is restored after teardown failure
+Flask MUST restore context-local state before a deferred teardown failure
+leaves a request or application context.
+
+#### Scenario: Context pop reports cleanup failures
+- **WHEN** teardown raises one or more deferred failures while popping a context
+- **THEN** no application or request context remains active after the error is
+  caught
